.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The board analysis reveals a critical defensive situation for Black. White has stones positioned at G4, G6, G7, and G8. This configuration leaves a single gap at G5. If White were to play at G5, it would connect these stones to form a vertical 5-in-a-row, resulting in an immediate win for White. Black currently has several blocked 4-in-a-rows (e.g., Row 6, Row 9, and two diagonals), but none can be converted into a win (5-in-a-row) in a single move. In Gomoku, an immediate threat of 5-in-a-row by the opponent takes precedence over any non-winning threats (like creating a 4) by the player. Therefore, Black is forced to play defensively.\n\nReason: White has a winning threat in column G (G4, G6, G7, G8). Black must play G5 to block White from completing the 5-in-a-row and winning the game immediately.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "G", "row": 5}'}
