 at both ends by White (O) stones. Consequently, Black has no immediate way to form 5-in-a-row or create a lethal "Live 4" or "4-3" combination. However, White has a very dangerous configuration on Row 7 with stones at G7, H7, and I7. This is a "Sleeping 3". If White is allowed to play at F7, they will create a "Sleeping 4" (F7-G7-H7-I7) which is blocked at J7 but open at E7. This would allow White to play E7 on the following turn to complete 5-in-a-row and win. Since Black has no forcing win to execute first, Black\'s absolute priority is to block this threat.\n\nReason: White has a potential winning line on Row 7 (G7-H7-I7). If White plays F7, they create a 4-in-a-row with an open end at E7, leading to a win. Black must block this spot immediately to stay in the game.\n\nAnswer: { "col": "F", "row": 7 }'}
